e15c8f88-c56b-4e3d-acf6-e8494cf9dde5-0
00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:27.640
I think that's really big for the group
to understand and distinguish.

fbef8eb2-4ae2-47b0-a85c-a355c15c398c-0
00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:29.600
Let's start with challenging event.

47a6a664-81d6-4777-b150-e426f164d18b-0
00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:34.950
A challenging event is difficult in a
session moment when when your patient or

47a6a664-81d6-4777-b150-e426f164d18b-1
00:20:34.950 --> 00:20:37.998
or the person you're you're therapy with
is,

47a6a664-81d6-4777-b150-e426f164d18b-2
00:20:37.998 --> 00:20:41.520
is having a difficult session a
challenging moment?

23bdb366-e3a8-4fea-8ec0-acbf390541ca-0
00:20:41.520 --> 00:20:43.772
Again,
it should be defined and that's what

23bdb366-e3a8-4fea-8ec0-acbf390541ca-1
00:20:43.772 --> 00:20:46.280
we're saying here is,
is this is for discussion.

6f844e31-606f-408e-a7af-62ad824d9868-0
00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:51.675
A difficult in the session moment often
therapeutically productive,

6f844e31-606f-408e-a7af-62ad824d9868-1
00:20:51.675 --> 00:20:55.880
but it's distinguished by absence of
objective harm.

6b0e5d93-48c2-45b9-b4fc-5a77418118ae-0
00:20:56.640 --> 00:20:58.480
And then what is an adverse event?

5fca99d5-19f6-4f6f-b58f-94cd4530340a-0
00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:03.500
We were saying that adverse event
definition would be an outcome involving

5fca99d5-19f6-4f6f-b58f-94cd4530340a-1
00:21:03.500 --> 00:21:08.520
measurable clinical pathology and again
that would be with objective harm.

7cb5ddcf-8945-4877-98c0-d9711f952dd0-0
00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:15.054
And so a challenging event could be fear,
grief, anxiety, confusion, side effects,

7cb5ddcf-8945-4877-98c0-d9711f952dd0-1
00:21:15.054 --> 00:21:18.966
nausea, vomiting,
other things like that could be

7cb5ddcf-8945-4877-98c0-d9711f952dd0-2
00:21:18.966 --> 00:21:22.800
challenging in the moment versus adverse
events.

f2573de6-204b-486f-8219-ff169e1611ed-0
00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:28.880
An adverse event could be something that
is a cardiac event, a serotonin syndrome,

f2573de6-204b-486f-8219-ff169e1611ed-1
00:21:28.880 --> 00:21:32.591
which is very rare,
maybe an HPBD very rare again,

f2573de6-204b-486f-8219-ff169e1611ed-2
00:21:32.591 --> 00:21:34.120
or a psychotic break.

85f5d154-7be3-456e-ba27-676f7b7ed386-0
00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:36.320
Those would be adverse events.

5b8a889d-d696-437e-82fd-89b04dac2ea1-0
00:21:38.320 --> 00:21:40.160
And so that's what we wanted to kind of
do.

